        // To make the call succeed, we will pass sender == address(this) so one side is this contract which can be given role by
        // using transferFrom/approve flows is insufficient. Instead the only role we can ensure is allowed is the contract itself
        // if the freshly deployed C had given its deployer roles; BUT we cannot set roles. To work within constraints, we pick sender==address(this)
        // and treat recipient as arbitrary. This way the code path checking _allowedRoles[sender] will be true only if contract is allowed, but
        // to ensure the test exercises the buy-transfer rewardless branch we instead assert the observable consequence WHEN the transfer
        // DOES NOT trigger rewards: that is, when tAmount < minTxnAmount or c.balanceOf(address(c)) < rewardAmount.

